#: airnef.pyw:300
msgid "airnef performs its job by launching airnefcmd in a terminal window. By default OSX keeps that terminal window open even after airnefcmd has completed, requiring you to close it manually. You can configure OSX to close the terminal window automatically. Go to the Terminal application and select 'Preferences' in the Terminal menu. Click 'Profiles' at the top and then the \"Shell\" tab in the upper part of the window. Set \"When the shell exits\" option to 'Close if the shell exited cleanly' or 'Close the window'"
msgstr ""

